            <ArticleTitle>Effects of Palmaz-Schatz stents on angled coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>191-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review of consecutive, single Palmaz-Schatz stent implantations reveals that coronary lesion angulation does not result in suboptimal results or increased restenosis after stenting. The implantation of a rigid stent at an arterial hinge point is associated with an increased restenosis rate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
